From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the host BIOS updateable in Redfish

/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory/bios_active reported
"Updateable": false while bmc_active reported true, even though the host BIOS
is flashed through exactly the same Redfish multipart push as the BMC (and is,
in practice, updated that way regularly).

bmcweb defaults Updateable to false and only sets it true for objects that
appear in the /xyz/openbmc_project/software/updateable association.
ItemUpdater::createUpdateableAssociation() exists and is called for BMC images,
but createBIOSObject() only creates the active and functional associations, so
the BIOS object never joins it.

Add the missing call.  This is purely descriptive -- it corrects what the
service advertises about itself; the BIOS update path is unchanged.

--- a/item_updater.cpp
+++ b/item_updater.cpp
@@ -869,6 +869,11 @@
 
     createActiveAssociation(path);
     createFunctionalAssociation(path);
+    // Without this the BIOS object never joins
+    // /xyz/openbmc_project/software/updateable, so bmcweb leaves
+    // FirmwareInventory/bios_active "Updateable": false even though the host
+    // BIOS is updatable through exactly the same Redfish push as the BMC.
+    createUpdateableAssociation(path);
 
     auto versionId = path.substr(pos + 1);
     // Restore the version recorded by the last BIOS flash rather than
